{"tool_name":"stringmlst","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"stringmlst","identifiers":["biotools:stringmlst","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btw586"],"license":"Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International Public License","summary":"Fast k-mer based tool for multi locus sequence typing (mlst) directly from genome sequencing reads","home_url":"https://github.com/jordanlab/stringMLST","keywords":["Bacteria","Bacterial Typing Techniques","Campylobacter jejuni","Chlamydia trachomatis","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Multilocus Sequence Typing","Neisseria meningitidis","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Streptococcus pneumoniae","DNA","Assembly","Sequencing"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"stringmlst","home":"http://jordan.biology.gatech.edu/page/software/stringmlst/index.html","summary":"stringMLST is a tool for detecting the MLST of an isolate directly from the genome sequencing reads. stringMLST predicts the ST of an isolate in a completely assembly and alignment free manner.","addition_date":"2017-12-18T00:15:41Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-07T10:34:19.548191Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:stringmlst","credit":[{"email":"king.jordan@biology.gatech.edu","name":"Support","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://jordan.biology.gatech.edu/page/index.html"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://jordan.biology.gatech.edu/page/software/stringmlst/README.txt"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["rlibouban"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2928"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"stringMLST","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw586","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 The Author 2016. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.Rapid and accurate identification of the sequence type (ST) of bacterial pathogens is critical for epidemiological surveillance and outbreak control. Cheaper and faster next-generation sequencing (NGS) technologies have taken preference over the traditional method of amplicon sequencing for multilocus sequence typing (MLST). But data generated by NGS platforms necessitate quality control, genome assembly and sequence similarity searching before an isolate's ST can be determined. These are computationally intensive and time consuming steps, which are not ideally suited for real-time molecular epidemiology. Here, we present stringMLST, an assembly- and alignment-free, lightweight, platform-independent program capable of rapidly typing bacterial isolates directly from raw sequence reads. The program implements a simple hash table data structure to find exact matches between short sequence strings (k-mers) and an MLST allele library. We show that stringMLST is more accurate, and order of magnitude faster, than its contemporary genome-based ST detection tools.","authors":[{"name":"Gupta A."},{"name":"Jordan I.K."},{"name":"Rishishwar L."}],"citationCount":33,"date":"2017-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"stringMLST: A fast k-mer based tool for multilocus sequence typing"},"pmid":"27605103","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"},{"term":"DNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0654"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"stringMLST","home":"https://bio.tools/stringmlst","summary":"stringMLST is a tool for detecting the MLST of an isolate directly from the genome sequencing reads. stringMLST predicts the ST of an isolate in a completely assembly and alignment free manner.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:stringmlst/cmd/j